Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:20:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 242/402] Assembly: put parts in without being stopped to save
 or to ground

An unsaved assembly is saved to a provisional place (user data/Unsaved)
instead of the English "must be saved" message; it stays marked modified,
and Save asks for the place as for a new document. A part of a document
that was never saved (an opened STEP file) is copied into the assembly
rather than linked. The question whether to ground the first part, the
"inserted" counter and their buttons are translatable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
